{"translation": "Further, on the basis of the effects (ἔργα) which they are naturally disposed to produce, they have been said to have in them powers that are rarefying and condensing, softening and hardening, clogging and cleansing, drawing and repelling, and besides these relaxing, tightening, opening the mouths of vessels, contracting, thickening, thinning, anodyne, pain-causing, concocting, bringing to suppuration, dispersing, [711] sweat-inducing, stupefying, numbing, sleep-inducing, causing derangement, putrefying, burning, corroding, eschar-forming, liquefying, compacting, producing bad humours, tempering, purgative, checking, roughening, smoothing, obstructing and unblocking. And when they proceed still further and name them, as it were, individually after each of the effects, they call them diuretic, emetic, evacuant downward, laxative, errhine, phlegm-expelling, bringing on the menses or checking them. Likewise also either generative or extinguishing or provocative or retentive of milk and of semen. And still more, when they name certain powers hepatic or splenic or aural or ophthalmic or dental or sciatic or nephritic or podagric or arthritic or pleuritic or for cough or stone-breaking, they arrive at the particular powers. In the same way it has also been said that there is a flesh-forming power for an ulcer, and a scarring one, and an agglutinating and a removing one. Indeed, it is scarcely even possible to enumerate all the particular powers if we attempt to name them after each of the things they bring about.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 13, "surface": "ἀραιωτικάς", "english": "rarefying", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 16, "surface": "πυκνωτικὰς,", "english": "condensing", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 34, "surface": "συντατικὰς,", "english": "tightening", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 35, "surface": "ἀναστομωτικὰς,", "english": "opening the mouths of vessels", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 46, "surface": "ναρκωτικὰς,", "english": "numbing", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 56, "surface": "ἐπικεραστικὰς,", "english": "tempering", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 80, "surface": "λαπακτικὰς,", "english": "laxative", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 86, "surface": "ἐπισχετικάς.", "english": "checking", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["χυτικὰς", "πιλητικὰς", "ὑπακτικὰς", "καθαιρετικὴ", "ἐκστατικὰς"]}
```

