{"translation": "There must therefore be absolutely no astringent power at all in them, not even if the place or the affection should additionally require it. From this it is clear that sometimes they will in no way benefit the condition but will only soothe the pain, in which case they will also be called truly anodyne; but sometimes they will also give some additional benefit to the condition itself and will have a twofold power, being at the same time an anodyne [766] and a healing drug. These matters too will be discussed more fully in the books of the Therapeutic Method. For the present it is enough to explain that, of these drugs specifically named anodyne, some, as has been said, belong to the first rank of the heating drugs, and these are indeed truly anodyne, such as dill oil; others are [hot] to a degree close to that of our own body itself, such as those called suppurative, whose materials have been discussed earlier. Their use will be determined in the books of the Therapeutic Method. Those, however, that produce torpor when drunk, and for this reason are called anodyne and soporific by most people, are of a mixture most opposite to the truly anodyne drugs. For they all cool the body and numb sensation to such an extent that, if a little more is drunk, it brings on death. The best of them for the use in question are those that dry.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 47, "surface": "διττὴν,", "english": "twofold", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 65, "surface": "μεθόδου", "english": "Method", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 77, "surface": "ἀνωδύνων", "english": "anodyne", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 81, "surface": "ἔνια", "english": "some", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 132, "surface": "καταφορὰν", "english": "torpor", "uncertain": "y"}, {"target_no": 138, "surface": "ἀνώδυνά", "english": "anodyne", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 141, "surface": "ὑπνωτικὰ", "english": "soporific", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 152, "surface": "ἀνωδύνοις.", "english": "truly anodyne drugs", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["καταφορὰν", "παραπλησίως αὐτῷ τῷ ἡμετέρῳ σώματι", "διαπυητικὰ"]}
```

