{"translation": "What the cause of the benefit is [781] will be stated in the treatise on the Therapeutic Method, in which we also go through everything else concerning the use of drugs, so that there is no need to lengthen the discussion here any further, except perhaps to remark briefly on the use of names which certain others of the more recent physicians introduced as innovators, and not least the so-called Methodists. For that they speak of certain 'checking' (stalticai) powers, that is, constricting, or drawing together, or repelling, or something else of that kind, is neither absurd nor obscure. But when they say that certain materials or powers are 'metasyncritic', what is said is neither clear nor true nor proper to their sect, since they claim to avoid the indication taken from dogmatic suppositions, for, they say, the apparent novelties suffice them. But that, when the pores of the body are turned aside from the natural state into the unnatural, certain affections arise according to the particular character of their alteration, is a dogmatic supposition.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 10, "surface": "μεθόδου", "english": "Method", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 54, "surface": "μεθοδικοί.", "english": "Methodists", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 58, "surface": "σταλτικάς", "english": "checking", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 77, "surface": "ἀσαφές.", "english": "obscure", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 96, "surface": "αἱρέσεως", "english": "sect", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 105, "surface": "δογματικῶν", "english": "dogmatic", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 118, "surface": "πόρων", "english": "pores", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 130, "surface": "ἰδιότητι", "english": "particular character", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["καινότητας (perhaps a corruption of κοινότητας, the Methodist 'commonalities'; translated as printed, 'novelties')", "μετασυγκριτικάς (technical Methodist term, transliterated as 'metasyncritic')", "τροπῆς ('alteration' / 'turning')"]}
```

