{"translation": "[684] For those people need things that are astringent and viscid, not things that cut and divide. These matters, however, already in some way touch upon the therapeutic method. Having now defined the power of the bitter flavours, and having said that they are cutting, thinning and cleansing, and clearly hot to such a degree that they do not yet burn, let us in our account go on once more to the pungent ones. And first let us say that they are strictly hot, then that they are corrosive, caustic, eschar-forming and colliquative: all such are so when applied to the skin. When taken inside the body, however, those that are most opposite in their whole substances to certain animals are all putrefying and deleterious to those animals. Those that are so only through the immoderation of their heat are ulcerating to the inner parts if they are coarse-particled and earthy. If they are fine-particled, they are diuretic and sudorific, and, to put it simply, cutting and dispersing.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 36, "surface": "λεπτυντικοὺς", "english": "thinning", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 49, "surface": "δριμεῖς", "english": "pungent", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 62, "surface": "διαβρωτικούς", "english": "corrosive", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 67, "surface": "ἐσχαρωτικοὺς", "english": "eschar-forming", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 89, "surface": "ἐναντιώτατα", "english": "most opposite", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 94, "surface": "σηπτικούς", "english": "putrefying", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 99, "surface": "δηλητηρίους", "english": "deleterious", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 123, "surface": "διουρητικούς", "english": "diuretic", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["συντηκτικούς", "ἀμετρίαν", "γλίσχρων"]}
```

